N1  - <p>BOINC-era (flagged): proves/explains conjectures from the project results file results_different_zeta_orders.pdf, announced June 2022 ("Using a new algorithm, The Ramanujan Machine discovered in June 2022 several conjectures that include different values of Riemann Zeta function"), i.e. after the BOINC project launch (October 2021) and within the Distributed Factorial Reduction period reported in Elimelech et al. (2024) as "running online since October 2021." The paper itself does not state whether those specific conjectures were volunteer-computed, so BOINC provenance is by project date, not by an explicit computation statement. Paper text states: "The Ramanujan Machine project detects new expressions related to constants of interest... In particular the project lists several conjectures concerning values of the ζ function. We show that many relations detected by the Ramanujan Machine Project stem from a specific algebraic observation and show how to generate and machine-prove infinitely many. This provides an automated proof and/or an explanation of many of the relations listed as conjectures by the project"; worked example: "The Ramanujan Machine identity ζ(4) + 4ζ(3) − 8."</p>
